[TEXT] I now have complete, direct evidence. The picture is clear:

**BGP configs on both leaf routers have no `maximum-paths` directive.** BGP on leaf_router_0_0 sees *2 paths available* to 10.0.1.0/24 (one via each spine) but without `maximum-paths`, FRR only installs the *best* path into the FIB — selected by Router-ID tiebreaker (172.16.0.1 for spine_router_0_0 beats 172.16.0.3 for spine_router_0_1). All traffic funnels through spine_router_0_0 only. The same applies symmetrically on leaf_router_0_1. The super_spine receiving 0 prefixes from spine_router_0_0 is normal BGP AS-path loop prevention (not a fault).

